cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use TRIPWIRE, please cite this release. The data (reports/ and the generated dataset/) and the schemas
  are licensed CC BY 4.0; the code is licensed Apache-2.0.
title: "TRIPWIRE: A Dataset of Install-Time Environment Gates in Malicious npm and PyPI Packages"
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Syvendra
    given-names: Saai
    affiliation: University of Moratuwa
  - family-names: Samarakoon
    given-names: Himath
    affiliation: University of Moratuwa
  - family-names: Jegatheesan
    given-names: Kavienan
    affiliation: University of Moratuwa
  - family-names: Lihinikaduarachchi
    given-names: Gayathri
    affiliation: University of Moratuwa
  - family-names: Rathnayake
    given-names: Sunimal
    affiliation: University of Moratuwa
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-10
license: CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/saai-syvendra/TRIPWIRE"
abstract: >-
  Install-time environment gates in malicious npm and PyPI packages: for each campaign representative, every
  condition a package tests before its payload runs (API, compared value, boolean structure, smallest set that must
  hold together, environment recipe per branch), with hashed byte anchors into the package, member and skip records
  for denominators, verification verdicts from a deterministic checker and LLM reviewers, and the
  tools that rebuild every table without the malware.
keywords:
  - software supply chain
  - malicious packages
  - npm
  - PyPI
  - dynamic analysis
  - environment-sensitive malware
  - mining software repositories
